  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 242 AM MDT SAT AUG 29 2026\nThe long term period will feature an active and persistent \ntrough pattern across the western United States. An amplifying \ntrough off the Pacific Northwest coast will push another \nshortwave disturbance inland on Tuesday, bringing increased \nchances for showers and thunderstorms, mainly across the higher \nterrain.\n\nA stronger closed low will dig along the trough axis Wednesday\nthrough Friday, stalling near the Pacific Northwest coast. This\npositioning will keep southeast Oregon and southwest Idaho under\ncool, unsettled southwesterly flow aloft. High temperatures will\nfall roughly 10 degrees below normal for early September, with\nvalley highs remaining in the 70s. Tightening surface pressure\ngradients and strong mid level winds mixing down each afternoon\nwill generate widespread breezy to windy conditions Tuesday\nthrough Saturday. Shower and thunderstorm timing will remain\ntied to minor individual shortwaves rotating around the parent\ntrough.",
